        {
          "id": 431382713,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "PDML and PSML (which I'd forgotten even existed!) both include encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\".\n\nI really don't know much about utf-8 at all.  In the example file I was testing, some escaping is taking place, e.g.\n<field name=\"tcp.flags.str\" showname=\"TCP Flags: \\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7A\\xc2\\xb7R\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\" size=\"2\" pos=\"46\" show=\"\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7A\\xc2\\xb7R\\xc2\\xb7\\xc2\\xb7\" value=\"5014\"/>\n\nIn the GUI,  this field shows 12 characters, each one representing a bit - not-set flags are shown as a '.'.\n\nI don't know how users of PDML output would take to changes in behaviour - from the talk yesterday on Ostinato they seem to apply a few workarounds (he mentioned some field offsets / lengths not being correct I think).\n\nI am inclined to submit something that is functionally equivalent to the existing code (I need to check it over again), then work out whether it is safe to get rid of the other character escapting?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-10-17T22:23:33.064Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-10-17T22:23:33.064Z",
