    {
      "id": "f5e146a49677d7f1fae162cb6b714408740099d6",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 431726310,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Srivats P says (on Discord, of Ostinato):\n\"I checked the code. There's no explicit parsing of escaped characters in the PDML reading code. There is a chance that QT's xml/string parsing code may internally be parsing them without the application knowing about it but it should be able to parse the un-escaped versions also in that case I guess as per the spec.\"\n\nI think it is the right thing to do, but would still like to do it as a separate change.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
